      "title": "Kelvedon Hatch Secret Nuclear Bunker",
      "description": "ROTOR air defence control bunker converted to a Regional Seat of Government",
      "extract": "The Kelvedon Hatch Secret Nuclear Bunker at Kelvedon Hatch, in the Borough of Brentwood in the English county of Essex, is a large underground bunker maintained during the Cold War as a potential regional government headquarters. Since being decommissioned in 1992, the bunker has been open to the public as a tourist attraction, with a museum focusing on its Cold War history.",
